<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>3D-Printed Parts on brainboxemb</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/3d-parts/</link><description>Recent content in 3D-Printed Parts on brainboxemb</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/3d-parts/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Hinge Ideas</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/3d-parts/hinges/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/3d-parts/hinges/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This page collects &lt;strong&gt;3D-printable hinge ideas and real-world mechanism references&lt;/strong&gt; for the HUB75 display enclosure.&lt;/p&gt;
